\title{An execution that sends slices on a clock, each sized by the volume profile of the half hour it falls in}
\description{
The \code{vwap} execution of a plan: slices sized by how busy the market usually is, a volume-weighted average price order.

It sends \code{slices}, from 2 to 60, on the same clock as \code{TwapExecution}, but each slice takes the weight of the half hour it falls in, so slices near the busy open and close are bigger. The half hours are counted from the segment's own open, 09:15 for equity and 09:00 for currency and MCX, on the day the order starts working, and a slice after the last half hour takes the last weight. \code{volume_profile} gives the weights, one per half hour from the open; without it, an equity order takes UBI's NSE equity shape and a currency or commodity order gets even slices. Slices are whole lots, and a slice that comes to nothing is skipped.

The span is given in one of two ways: \code{over_minutes}, or \code{until}, a time of day such as \code{"15:00"}, which spreads the slices from when the order starts until that time and is refused if the order starts after it. Giving both is refused. A VWAP can be the outer or the inner execution of a nested pair, and cannot carry a resting stop.
}
